  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_99cee8cf236a4097a5eb682aaca3cf45",
      "statement": "celld is an alpha 'not safe for hostile multi-tenant use': it trusts the application code, fleet nodes, and operators, and depends on two external boundaries — a trusted private network for the internal listener and bucket credentials scoped to one fleet bucket.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L1-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:44a43dd2b285c55dccf0bebc6ed95b398d93e0a9864a0464bb00aafe2c3e7ebf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d79de76a2fe84211ac09320cb2996015",
      "statement": "The public Worker listener reserves only /.well-known/celld/health (200 {\"ok\":true} or 503); the Worker owns every other public path; the internal listener returns 404 for unknown paths rather than routing them to the Worker, defaulting to 127.0.0.1:0.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L22-L34",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a1879fe3a78a4dcb7972057ef53ce58c40df42b9956dbbfc2f0c9a65c2ce7bf9:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L40-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3cc2403658636b9ff07cbea831bace11b16cf0a8f2a2664358bf0746764d3965:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_db03044d84484bf1b4f9cb746ada43a0",
      "statement": "The internal listener has three request groups: unauthenticated operator routes, HMAC-authenticated /peer/tunnel establishment (inner tunneled calls are plain HTTP and unsigned), and HMAC-authenticated peer-control/reserved-cell routes; all three require the trusted private network.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L55-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:691505e18e05a1446b8d91f749ebd483d3d10b64914117d05f77340791194625:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_56eb6adf0ba94536961ed5a7be02141a",
      "statement": "The fleet secret is a 32-byte key stored at fleet/peer-auth.json with a version envelope; load_or_create bootstraps it via a conditional create so exactly one node creates it, and a lost create race resolves by re-reading the stored secret.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L196-L197",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6362d1fd6763f6afedd19338859e94ad5b8de9bf70cd07a809c641908cc695a3:"
